    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac00434e_1ae75fc4",
        "filename": "board/cr50/rdd.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 140,
      "author": {
        "id": 1283719
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-17T21:29:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "GC_IRQNUM_UART2_TXINT irq will call get_data_from_usb(); (by chip/g/usart.h).\nget_data_from_usb() moves data from USB data queue to UART TX.\n\nI just got the second thought, like the case that UART_EC has been always enabled (since CCD_CAP_GSC_TX_EC_RX is enabled), then uartn_tx_connect() shall never be called because delta bit is zero. GC_IRQNUM_UART2_TXINT should be triggered at the end of ccd_state_change_hook() if uart_tx_is_connected(UART_EC) is true.",
      "parentUuid": "dd105aaa_03ce337f",
      "revId": "450f586891f923d0666e2066fadb2330fbb21848",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e36c9ed_132a7a91",
        "filename": "board/cr50/rdd.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 256,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-01-17T19:13:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This tells you if EC TX CR50 RX is allowed. You need to keep only enabling EC RX if CCD_ENABLE_UART_EC is set here. \nIf you always enable RX when ec_comm_is_uart_in_packet_mode, then there will be interrupt storms on Cr50 when EC TX CR50 RX isn\u0027t pulled up (This happens on some boards when the EC enters hibernate).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 256,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 256,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "450f586891f923d0666e2066fadb2330fbb21848",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
